# Accepted-risk signal-disposition sites excluded from the ownership gate.
#
# Format: file:line:hash  # rationale
#   file    = repo-relative path
#   line    = line number of the flagged call as reported by the scanner
#   hash    = first 8 hex chars of sha256 of the both-ends-trimmed line
#             content (leading and trailing whitespace stripped)
#
# Keying on file:line:hash means both the line number AND the site text
# must match.  A renumber or text edit without re-auditing fails on hash
# mismatch.  A new install call added elsewhere in an allowlisted file is
# still caught.
#
# PRE-EMPTIVE EXEMPTIONS (no active allowlist key — documented here so
# contributors know these sites are already reviewed):
#
#   childops/misc/fork-storm.c:117
#     Whole-table SIG_DFL reset inside sanitize_grandchild_signals().
#     raise(SIGUSR1) is in do_exit_as(), a separate function called after
#     sanitize_grandchild_signals() returns.  The two-line proximity
#     window correctly excludes this cross-function pattern.  No active
#     allowlist key needed; site is inherently outside check1 scope.
#
#   childops/misc/pidfd-storm.c:169
#     Same pattern: whole-table SIG_DFL reset in a grandchild sanitizer,
#     no raise() within any reachable 2-line window.  Correct by design;
#     no allowlist key required.

